      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T15:45:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should first focus on the purpose of this new entry (\"why would I use it?\") instead of how it\u0027s been implemented. In particular, the DT node is one way to communicate the region to the guest but, depending on the platform, the support might be extended to other firmware formats.\n\nI\u0027d recommend something along the lines of\n\n\u003e entry 4 if present contains potentially confidential data to be passed to specific guests, identified from their VM name. If the data is confidential, this feature should only be used with guests using a fixed rollback protection mechanism, to prevent rollback attacks from a malicious host. Data is passed as a `reserved-memory` region through the device tree, with the provided properties, at an address which is implementation defined. Multiple regions may be passed to the same guest.\n\nthen you can proceed with the actual low-level format.",
