      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T15:45:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why? This prevents the layout mentioned in b/382493676#comment2, using a string table at the end, and instead forces duplicating the `compatible` string between entries that could share it.\n\nYou could simply check that the \"blobs\" are non-overlapping and in-order (not necessary but easier to implement):\n```\nuse vmbase::util::RangeExt as _;\n```\n```\nlet mut last_blob_end \u003d 0;\nfor hdr in hdrs {\n    let limits \u003d last_blob_end..buffer.len();\n    lef offset \u003d hdr.blob_offset();\n    let blob \u003d offset..(offset + hdr.blob_size());\n    if !blob.is_within(\u0026limits) {\n        return Err(...);\n    }\n    last_blob_end \u003d blob.end;\n}\n```\nthen that all strings (`compat` and `vm_name`) are after `last_blob_end`. Note that it isn\u0027t an issue (and is actually a feature) if the string offsets point to (partially) overlapping strings.",
