      "writtenOn": "2025-02-12T23:53:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FWIW you\u0027re correct that the intermediate types aren\u0027t needed - this could be written with [`iter::from_fn`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/fn.from_fn.html) and have something like this:\n\n```rust\nfn iter_resmem_entries(buffer: \u0026\u0027a [u8]) -\u003e Result\u003cimpl Iterator\u003cItem \u003d ConfigHeaderEntry\u003c\u0027a\u003e\u003e\n```\n\nIt\u0027d be essentially the same thing except the iteration state is tracked in `move`d closure variables instead of a struct fields. Short example:\n\n```rust\npub fn evens(in_range: Range\u003cu32\u003e) -\u003e impl Iterator\u003cItem \u003d u32\u003e {\n    let mut i \u003d in_range.start.wrapping_sub(2);\n    std::iter::from_fn(move || {\n        i \u003d i.wrapping_add(2);\n        (i \u003c in_range.end).then_some(i)\n    })\n}\n```\n\nI\u0027ve no problem with some intermediate types though.",
      "parentUuid": "e4e85561_32ceb539",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "7f485c77428d523f170e4dbdcd91140016af83b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
